2. In addition to the powers conferred upon him by other rules the Registrar shall have the following duties and powers in relation to civil and criminal matters:
(1) to receive an appeal under C1. 15 of the Letters Patent from the judgment ofa Division Court, and to issue notices as soon as the appeal is registered;
(2) to receive an appeal under C1. 15 of the Letters Patent from the judgment ofa Judge sitting singly, and to post it for hearing;
(3) to receive an appeal from an original or appellate decree or order of a Subordinate Civil Court, and if in order to post it for hearing under Order XLI, R. 11 ofthe Civil Procedure Code;
(4)todisposeofallmattersrelatingtoCourt-fees(otherthanappealsthe subject-matter of which is the amount of Court-fee payable) and to the service of notices or other processes;
Provided that rules in which a returmable date has beenfixed by theBench and in which there has been default in paying the process fee within the time allowed by the second proviso to R. 12 of Chapter IV of these rules shall be laid before theBench,dealingwith Lawazima matters;
(5) to dispose of all matters relating - (i) to the substitution of the heirs of parties provided no question of limitation arises, (i) to the representation of minor parties when there is no dispute as to guardianship, and (ii) applications under
